{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon","id":550434,"title":"Namtaru Can Teleport to the Moon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-11T11:44:20-07:00","id":550434,"title":"Namtaru Can Teleport to the Moon?","content":"I've been reading the Kickstarter preview of the rules, and it seems the Shadow Soul Atavism is overpowered.<br /> <br /> The Low Satiety power lets you extend from senses out from any patch of shadow connected from the one you are in, and has unfettered awareness in darkness.<br /> <br /> The Satiety expenditure power lets you teleport to any shadow you can see from the rest of the scene, and this power explicitly is said to stack with the Low Satiety power.<br /> <br /> So if I'm in the countryside, I could extend my senses across the ocean, see a shadow in Africa, Portugal, or the UK, and hop right over instantly. While this doesn't apply during the day, and maybe not on full moons, and not in cities, where the contiguous shadows are brief, it does basically give me the power to go globe hopping with relative ease.<br /> <br /> Taking this to an extreme, the part of the moon that isn't shining is in the shadow of the Earth, so without even being low Satiety you could teleport from the Earth to the Moon (survival not guaranteed).<br /> <br /> And that basically takes away the pressure of the hunt. I mean, I when sun sets on the East coast of North America, pretty much all of Europe and Africa are in night. A Namtaru could hunt in a different country every day. A Beast could cherry pick anyone on four continents (Europe, Africa, North America, South America), and find the perfect targets, and if any heroes are created, good luck finding the Beast!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2466-divine-virus","name":"Divine Virus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:31:36-07:00","id":550550,"title":"","content":"Well, only if you allow it.<br /> From a physical perpective, the absence of light is darkness, which is the same as shadow, but thats not nessesarily true in a metaphysical sense. Night doesn't nessesarily qualify as shadows for the purposes of this and simmilar abillities unless you want them to. It would be very easy to rule that night is merely the natural absence of light while shadow is the act of preventing light from shineing on something. The Beast doesn't have an affinity with shadows and darkness, but rather with the act of depriving light from shineing on something. Light has a rightful connotation of life and loveliness in many cultures, so it would be thematically apropriate for the Beast to have an affinity with the act of depriving an area of this loveliness, rather than the actual physical decrease of photons.<br /> <br /> Be alittle creative and you can housewhole whatever you want. If you give an aproriate in-universe reason as to why this is the case, your players wont mind, especially if the reason is cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:25:05-07:00","id":550603,"title":"","content":"I would argue that night is not a shadow, so you can't do massive jumps just on the grounds of it is night on this part of the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:27:35-07:00","id":550619,"title":"","content":"There are a tonne of ways to fix it with house rules, but I wanted to point out that RAW, this is all clearly possible. This needs to be specifically house ruled against unless you want Beasts who can globe trot with impunity. It also makes the Shadowed Soul atavism pretty unbalanced compared to its peers.<br /> <br /> As for my game, we've ruled that one only has unlimited teleportation on new moons and lunar eclipses. If there is even a sliver of a moon, teleportation is limited to Lairx10 miles, and one cannot cross or spy over rivers, oceans, or lakes, as the like reflecting on the water effectively makes it not &quot;shadow&quot; or &quot;dark.&quot; Lastly, interstates and other major highways with overlapping lights breaks cannot be spied across, because they break up the country into smaller chunks of shadow, like walls of light.<br /> <br /> So there are abundant fixes, but the problem is that a fix is necessary in the first place. That everything I described is possible, RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2466-divine-virus","name":"Divine Virus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:34:04-07:00","id":550620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550550#post550550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, only if you allow it.<br /> From a physical perpective, the absence of light is darkness, which is the same as shadow, but thats not nessesarily true in a metaphysical sense. Night doesn't nessesarily qualify as shadows for the purposes of this and simmilar abillities unless you want them to. It would be very easy to rule that night is merely the natural absence of light while shadow is the act of preventing light from shineing on something. The Beast doesn't have an affinity with shadows and darkness, but rather with the act of depriving light from shineing on something. Light has a rightful connotation of life and loveliness in many cultures, so it would be thematically apropriate for the Beast to have an affinity with the act of depriving an area of this loveliness, rather than the actual physical decrease of photons.<br /> <br /> Be alittle creative and you can housewhole whatever you want. If you give an aproriate in-universe reason as to why this is the case, your players wont mind, especially if the reason is cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>This post made me think of Namtaru finding solar eclipses to be truly joyous events, as as an eclipse would enable long range sensing and teleportation. That the people are distracted by the eclipse itself is a nice bonus. The best moment to turn that wonder into fear. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:41:25-07:00","id":550625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550620#post550620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This post made me think of Namtaru finding solar eclipses to be truly joyous events, as as an eclipse would enable long range sensing and teleportation. That the people are distracted by the eclipse itself is a nice bonus. The best moment to turn that wonder into fear. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Suddenly, Tzitzimime-based Namtaru became a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:01:39-07:00","id":550667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Divine Virus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550619#post550619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a tonne of ways to fix it with house rules, but I wanted to point out that RAW, this is all clearly possible. This needs to be specifically house ruled against unless you want Beasts who can globe trot with impunity. It also makes the Shadowed Soul atavism pretty unbalanced compared to its peers.<br /> <br /> As for my game, we've ruled that one only has unlimited teleportation on new moons and lunar eclipses. If there is even a sliver of a moon, teleportation is limited to Lairx10 miles, and one cannot cross or spy over rivers, oceans, or lakes, as the like reflecting on the water effectively makes it not &quot;shadow&quot; or &quot;dark.&quot; Lastly, interstates and other major highways with overlapping lights breaks cannot be spied across, because they break up the country into smaller chunks of shadow, like walls of light.<br /> <br /> So there are abundant fixes, but the problem is that a fix is necessary in the first place. That everything I described is possible, RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you're capping a houserule.The RAW only spells out that one can make great jumps if they can play it properly, but it doesn't say that night is a massive shadow and would thus allow for that.<br /> <br /> The eclipse thing though would be pretty cool though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:25:39-07:00","id":550706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550620#post550620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This post made me think of Namtaru finding solar eclipses to be truly joyous events, as as an eclipse would enable long range sensing and teleportation. That the people are distracted by the eclipse itself is a nice bonus. The best moment to turn that wonder into fear. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>A monster that patiently awaits the masking of the sun, to go hunting its prey across the entire earth?<br /> Yep. Sounds like a monster story to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:54:41-07:00","id":550761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550667#post550667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually you're capping a houserule.The RAW only spells out that one can make great jumps if they can play it properly, but it doesn't say that night is a massive shadow and would thus allow for that.<br /> <br /> The eclipse thing though would be pretty cool though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The solar eclipse thing would be super cool.<br /> <br /> As for night being a massive shadow, that is literally what the night is. At night, we are in the shadow of the earth. That's not a poetic interpretation but a literal truth.<br /> <br /> Also, I just realized, the shadow doesn't need to be dark enough to conceal you, only contain you. Which means during the day, when its overcast, you could similarly go freely hopping around under the cloud's shadow.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2466-divine-virus","name":"Divine Virus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:04:02-07:00","id":550774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Divine Virus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550761#post550761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The solar eclipse thing would be super cool.<br /> <br /> As for night being a massive shadow, that is literally what the night is. At night, we are in the shadow of the earth. That's not a poetic interpretation but a literal truth.<br /> <br /> Also, I just realized, the shadow doesn't need to be dark enough to conceal you, only contain you. Which means during the day, when its overcast, you could similarly go freely hopping around under the cloud's shadow.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is the time when the part of the earth you're on is not facing the sun which would be not a shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:04:02-07:00","id":550775,"title":"","content":"And, also, Does the Shadow count as a shadow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:11:10-07:00","id":550780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550775#post550775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, also, Does the Shadow count as a shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol that would be such a glorious dick move. &quot;We're in the Shadow, so I'm basically omnipresent.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:30:55-07:00","id":550817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550774#post550774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is the time when the part of the earth you're on is not facing the sun which would be not a shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Night is recognized by science as being in the Earth's shadow. You can check the wikipedia page (crtl-F &quot;shadow&quot; for ease).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/1280px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night\" target=\"_blank\"> Night - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2466-divine-virus","name":"Divine Virus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:42:12-07:00","id":550827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Divine Virus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550817#post550817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Night is recognized by science as being in the Earth's shadow. You can check the wikipedia page (crtl-F &quot;shadow&quot; for ease).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the Begotten's powers work off of, to quote somebody else on this forum (can't recall who), Astral symbolism, much like a Mage's power works off of Supernal symbolism. Symbolically, Night and Shadow are two distinct (but related) concepts, so the question is whether the two concepts are considered similar enough Astrally to be considered the same for this power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:29:42-07:00","id":550955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550827#post550827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the Begotten's powers work off of, to quote somebody else on this forum (can't recall who), Astral symbolism, much like a Mage's power works off of Supernal symbolism. Symbolically, Night and Shadow are two distinct (but related) concepts, so the question is whether the two concepts are considered similar enough Astrally to be considered the same for this power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I am talking about the Rules As Written. I haven't gone through the book with a fine tooth comb, but I haven't seen it said Beasts work of Astral Symbolism. I think its likely that many people picking up the book won't know that. Even then, given that low satiety power for Shadowed Soul works explicitly in any darkness (not just shadow) I think it cannot be assumed that Shadow and Night are wholly distinct in Astral Symbolism.<br /> <br /> I am not trying to defend this, and say Namtaru should be able to teleport to the moon or globe hope. I am saying that RAW, those with Shadowed Soul can do this, using the standard definition of shadow (I mean, I learned the night was the earth's shadow in grade 7). And I think its probably unbalanced that Shadow Soul allows that, and maybe it should be tweaked in the final draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2466-divine-virus","name":"Divine Virus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:44:29-07:00","id":550968,"title":"","content":"This reminds me of people complaining about some of the demon powers people were complaining knockout punch was to strong not sure if they changed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T21:10:50-07:00","id":551056,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it. Sometimes Beasts just disappear and the moon isn't a safe place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T21:53:11-07:00","id":551091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=551056#post551056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd allow it. Sometimes Beasts just disappear and the moon isn't a safe place.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and if the power where beast can eavesdrop the world actually tries it the person would probably be driven insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T03:39:19-07:00","id":551226,"title":"","content":"Just make sure you have &quot;suffocating&quot; as a lair trait first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T03:51:35-07:00","id":551231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Divine Virus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550955#post550955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, I am talking about the Rules As Written. I haven't gone through the book with a fine tooth comb, but I haven't seen it said Beasts work of Astral Symbolism. I think its likely that many people picking up the book won't know that. Even then, given that low satiety power for Shadowed Soul works explicitly in any darkness (not just shadow) I think it cannot be assumed that Shadow and Night are wholly distinct in Astral Symbolism.<br /> <br /> I am not trying to defend this, and say Namtaru should be able to teleport to the moon or globe hope. I am saying that RAW, those with Shadowed Soul can do this, using the standard definition of shadow (I mean, I learned the night was the earth's shadow in grade 7). And I think its probably unbalanced that Shadow Soul allows that, and maybe it should be tweaked in the final draft.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You seem to the only person interpretting all of night in this game as a shadow. RAW does not say all of Night is single shadow. That's you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T04:35:26-07:00","id":551260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Divine Virus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550955#post550955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, I am talking about the Rules As Written. I haven't gone through the book with a fine tooth comb, but I haven't seen it said Beasts work of Astral Symbolism. I think its likely that many people picking up the book won't know that. Even then, given that low satiety power for Shadowed Soul works explicitly in any darkness (not just shadow) I think it cannot be assumed that Shadow and Night are wholly distinct in Astral Symbolism.<br /> <br /> I am not trying to defend this, and say Namtaru should be able to teleport to the moon or globe hope. I am saying that RAW, those with Shadowed Soul can do this, using the standard definition of shadow (I mean, I learned the night was the earth's shadow in grade 7). And I think its probably unbalanced that Shadow Soul allows that, and maybe it should be tweaked in the final draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is your Arguement? Cause all I'm seeing is that the Splat and Ability that lets you be an Eldritch Abomination shouldn't have a Power that let's them.. Well be Eldritch according too your responses. Does the power need abit of Clarifying? From what your saying, possibly but then again as others have pointed out, there is a Difference between Shadow and Night. Shadow's are Cast by Light, Night is Cast by the Absence of Light, or the Blocking of Light from the Moon, Yeah if your Scientific about it your right, but kinda missing the Mystical side of the power.<br /> <br /> Also pointed out... if someone does use the power too evesdrop on the whole planet... You WILL go nuts from all the voices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T05:50:45-07:00","id":551284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=551260#post551260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also pointed out... if someone does use the power too evesdrop on the whole planet... You WILL go nuts from all the voices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Superman does it from time to time and he doesn't go crazy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:31:28-07:00","id":551307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=551284#post551284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? Superman does it from time to time and he doesn't go crazy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Supes doesn't do it all the Time, He does it for afew Seconds and Stops, he Also has spent Years training it. If your just doing it without Training it you will be overwhelmed. When it first appeared he was overwhelmed and Needed someone too help him get used too it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:05:13-07:00","id":551367,"title":"","content":"So.... he developed some discipline and mental shields to keep the vast confluence at bay except when he wishes to willfully expose himself to it. And a Beast can't do this Why? I can see a Merit doing this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:12:52-07:00","id":551387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=551367#post551367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.... he developed some discipline and mental shields to keep the vast confluence at bay except when he wishes to willfully expose himself to it. And a Beast can't do this Why? I can see a Merit doing this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't say he Couldn't.. Just Not gonna have it Happen all at once. And i Wouldn't (Personally) let a Player Start with the Ability too filter it, atleast not right at the beginning. If it's one of the things they want with XP Sure. Merit it away, just.. No Starting/New Beast i'd let have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:24:08-07:00","id":551401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=551231#post551231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You seem to the only person interpretting all of night in this game as a shadow. RAW does not say all of Night is single shadow. That's you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm going to preface this with stating I don't think this power should encompass the entire night side of the planet.<br /> <br /> BUT: &quot;RAW does not say all of night is a single shadow. That's you.&quot; is REALLY shitty reasoning. As a matter of face, RAW not speaking as to whether night is a shadow <i>means that night is a shadow</i> because a lack of statement to the contrary means it defaults to how reality works. The way reality works is that standing outside at night puts you in the shadow of Earth. You can make all sorts of OTHER arguments -- night isn't shadow in Beast because Beast and it's powers work off of thematic words and thematically night is Night not Shadow or whatever. That's fine. But that argument is in addition to and in spite of the <i>fact</i> that nighttime is the Earth's shadow. Stating this isn't the case because RAW never says it is does some incredibly wonky stuff with every other game, since now RAW has to explicitly confirm scientific facts for those facts to be present in a game. For instance, note that vehicles don't have an &quot;average/maximum range&quot; in their statlines, which means they can drive forever now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:47:40-07:00","id":551455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Divine Virus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550619#post550619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a tonne of ways to fix it with house rules, but I wanted to point out that RAW, this is all clearly possible.</div> </div> </div> </div> Only if we agree with your reading. By a strict reading, no, the dark side of the moon is not a shadow. There's also the problem that you can't really <i>see</i> it. <br /> <br /> Throwing around &quot;Its the RAW!&quot; simply isn't true. You are throwing around your RAI, your interpretation of the rules, as if it was RAW. Its not shitty reasoning if someone disagrees with your particular reasoning. And that's where this is going - Enokh, you are insisting that your way of reading it is the only way to read it. And its not. Its not a &quot;house rule&quot; if you don't think jumping to the dark side of the moon is allowed by default.<br /> <br /> That's all I have to say on the matter. Enokh, your reading is clearly not universal, so we have to agree to disagree. And lets move on. Rules layering and sematics arguments are not helping anyone here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:56:18-07:00","id":551479,"title":"","content":"I think to qualify as in a shadow you need to be unable to look directly at any light sources bigger than, say, stars. Ergo, if you can see the moon, you're not in shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:18:22-07:00","id":551541,"title":"","content":"I though RAI meant &quot;Rules as Intended,&quot; and not &quot;Rules as Interpreted,&quot; or at least, that's how I normally see it used...<br /> <br /> About the night being a shadow: In common usage people do not consider the night to be a shadow. Or at least where I'm from we don't. It is just the night. This doesn't mean there are no shadows during the night, only that they need other light sources than the sun to be cast, such as the stars or the moon, or in modern times the diffusion of city lights on the clouds. So I'd argue that RAW is inconclusive, as multiple readings are possible. But I guess that if the night being one large shadow was intended, it would have been called out in the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:56:40-07:00","id":551909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=551401#post551401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to preface this with stating I don't think this power should encompass the entire night side of the planet.<br /> <br /> BUT: &quot;RAW does not say all of night is a single shadow. That's you.&quot; is REALLY shitty reasoning. As a matter of face, RAW not speaking as to whether night is a shadow <i>means that night is a shadow</i> because a lack of statement to the contrary means it defaults to how reality works.The way reality works is that standing outside at night puts you in the shadow of Earth. You can make all sorts of OTHER arguments -- night isn't shadow in Beast because Beast and it's powers work off of thematic words and thematically night is Night not Shadow or whatever. That's fine. But that argument is in addition to and in spite of the <i>fact</i> that nighttime is the Earth's shadow. Stating this isn't the case because RAW never says it is does some incredibly wonky stuff with every other game, since now RAW has to explicitly confirm scientific facts for those facts to be present in a game. For instance, note that vehicles don't have an &quot;average/maximum range&quot; in their statlines, which means they can drive forever now.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW night isn't a shadow because that's how ENGLISH works. You can say all sorts of &quot;Well science say x&quot; and yes its technically true. That's why the sciences have to redefine and use all sorts specialized words because common words do not work the same way. And no RAW does not have confirm scientific facts because its not a real world simulator. Just like super speed powers don't cause insane friction(or run into people) powers work as they are described and as described its clear shadows aren't night except to you and you alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:04:01-07:00","id":551922,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm fond of making powers punchy as all hell and creating consequences that complicate the story. Beasts already have a tremendous amount of mobility, as far as I understand, by utilizing the Primordial Pathways and their Chambers to hop between places that share those themes. Adjusting this Atavism, I'd probably just make the roll extended if you're trying to move somewhere more than 20 yards away or so, saying it takes you time to trace a path of shadow that's unbroken by some errant beam of moonlight. On a dark new moon, the world is your oyster so long as you take the time to concentrate. For kicks, I'd probably also say that moving through the shadows of the depths of the ocean is something dangerous. No telling what unspeakable things roam the abyss in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","name":"Tilting Clock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:09:49-07:00","id":552230,"title":"","content":"Night is the Earth casting it's shadow. However, the phases of the moon are caused by the moon's shadow. This means the only time the shadow of the Earth is connected to the moon is during a lunar eclipse, which requires the moon to be full. Normally, the blackness of space separates the moon from the Earth's shadow (night). When the moon is full, it casts light creating shadows on the Earth during night and I would say those supersede the shadow of night, as does the shadows created with artificial light. So I would not count night as a shadow unless there was no artificial light sources and the moon was in the new phase. That would mean you could never travel to the moon with that power. If it was a new moon and there was no artificial light around, go crazy porting around on the surface of the Earth. It is such a niche case, that I would be okay with it. If you can cast shadows within shadows then I say the lightest of umbras doesn't count. You can't have people using the moon being in the sky during day to travel around anywhere they can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:04:05-07:00","id":552304,"title":"","content":"If you count night as a shadow, then any natural darkness counts as shadow. In a dark closet? Well that's just the shadow of the door. Dark cave? Shadow of rock above you. Commonsense says if they wanted it to work like that at night they would have said so. Don't try to justify shanagins with, &quot; Well the books don't say it's not.&quot; Any time you have to tell your self that the books don't say you can't, pump the breaks and use some basic logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T12:53:26-07:00","id":553344,"title":"","content":"Technically, a dark cave is like space, just absence of light, not a proper shadow. I wouldn't consider it shanagins if allowing it to work in a dark cave. I also wouldn't expect many people to come up with the idea to port to the moon. I would allow it in the niche case that I mentioned; night, no moonlight, no artificial light. That means a couple nights a month you can move pretty freely as long as you stay in the middle of nowhere. I would allow it because otherwise I would make a hole which the power isn't effective. Since it is about embracing darkness, a hole related to darkness doesn't make much sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:10:15-07:00","id":553354,"title":"","content":"Caves work. That's specifically called out as something that gets you full awareness. I guess it's a claustrophobia thing or something. Dark cave, monster, y'know. It's thematic. Plus the whole lair thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:50:06-07:00","id":553373,"title":"","content":"Although, regardless, the Moon could make for a damn cool Chamber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:01:43-07:00","id":553398,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but I don't know if the traits cover micropressure, microgravity, freezing cold and no air. I think I wouldn't like trying to make those first two up. Too much of a headache to deal with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Heart could be &quot;on the moon.&quot; Since it would be nothing more than a dream version, it could have normal gravity and pressure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 06-13-2015, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:27:08-07:00","id":553411,"title":"","content":"Would they naturally include such concepts, though? Think... Final Fantasy IV, or example. You head to the moon in order to fight the way to the last boss in the game. There's little in the way of oxygen deprivation there.<br /> <br /> Its not a question of how scientific being on the moon can be, but what fits into the fantasy idea of eldritch evil moon bases.<br /> <br /> EDUT - YMMV, but I'd allow moon-based Lairs without all the deprivation, lack of gravity, etc, depending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:31:33-07:00","id":553414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=553398#post553398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but I don't know if the traits cover micropressure, microgravity, freezing cold and no air. I think I wouldn't like trying to make those first two up. Too much of a headache to deal with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Heart could be &quot;on the moon.&quot; Since it would be nothing more than a dream version, it could have normal gravity and pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extreme Cold and Suffocating already exist, and micropressure and microgravity wouldn't be too hard:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Vacuum:</b></u><br /> This area is a total or near-total vacuum. There is no air to breathe, and anyone caught in the area unprotected takes 1 Lethal Damage per turn. This damage can be downgraded by Vampiric damage resistance, as well as similar structurally-based damage downgrading. Machines don't suffer damage from this, nor do Demons in their Demonic form.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Microgravity:</u></b><br /> The gravity in this area is weak, but still present. All those in the area receive a +2 bonus to Athletics rolls to jump, as well as any Strength-based roll to oppose gravity (throwing something, jumping, lifting heavy things, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:39:07-07:00","id":553418,"title":"","content":"It sounds like a great Heart idea. I think having a Chamber that is actually connected to the Moon would be problematic. It would take some serious convincing. It would be a pain to create a Chamber on the Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:41:09-07:00","id":553419,"title":"","content":"Perhaps you could try for the astral version of the moon. That seems a lot more likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:32:04-07:00","id":553480,"title":"","content":"I'm not very familiar with the astral. I'm also not sure why anyone would really care to go to any version of the moon outside of their Lair. The problem with vacuum is you have about 2 minutes before you die. A more accurate representation would be 1 or 2 aggravated damage per turn. Having your blood boil tends to be a problem for anyone. You also have a Lair trait that can't be used effectively in most places. The Moon doesn't hold atmosphere, but it doesn't push it away, so the Vacuum would collapse in any area not capable of a vacuum seal, as the atmosphere rushed in to equalize the pressure. It is just wonky. I don't think creating vacuums is something that many people would allow in their game. Instant death tends to be viewed as overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:01:14-07:00","id":553496,"title":"","content":"With mages &quot;because I can&quot; is generally sufficient. With beasts, who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:22:14-07:00","id":553506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=553496#post553496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With mages &quot;because I can&quot; is generally sufficient. With beasts, who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div>A beast that could would probably have the same reasoning. Alternately, they heard rumours about Packet Theta and decided to investigate themselves, see if they could establish Kinship with such a purportedly powerful being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:37:26-07:00","id":554983,"title":"","content":"Vacuum would or ably just be modeled as a combo of Sufficatong and Crushing (i.e. Level 4 Extreme Environment). Then you have Extreme Cold/Heat for if the spot is currently in light or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:29:08-07:00","id":555796,"title":"","content":"This is the sort of thing that, while technically supported by science, would cause me to throw dice at the player trying to pull it. If it were meant to apply this way there would be some kind of note of that in the RAW and if there were I'd houserule it into a smoking crater anyway because it's freakin' stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T11:01:38-07:00","id":555859,"title":"","content":"Why should there be a note on commonly accepted scientific knowledge? The application of it may be ludicrous, but still...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T12:00:55-07:00","id":555896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=555859#post555859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should there be a note on commonly accepted scientific knowledge? The application of it may be ludicrous, but still...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because what the average person means in casual conversation by the word 'shadow' does not encompass the huge honking shadow of the Earth blotting out the Sun that we refer to as 'night'. We've got a separate word for it and everything. Although it is objectively just a big shadow it's rare that supernatural powers treat it that way. For instance, Vampires take damage from the sun even when they're standing in shadows, which by the logic employed here should mean that going outside EVER should kill them. (and in fact, many places inside as well.)<br /> <br /> There should be a note precisely <i>because</i> the application of it is ludicrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T12:58:25-07:00","id":555927,"title":"","content":"I suddenly feel the need to point out that despite my detailed analysis I was not accepting &quot;night&quot; as a &quot;shadow&quot; for the purposes of the power. I was explaining why even if you accept the ludicrous premise then you still fail. I say it works in a dark cave because it's dark. It works at night with a new moon and no lights for the same reason. That fits what seems to be the intention in a more narrow fashion than it is stated. I don't remember if the power states you have to see where you intend to go, but I would consider that the case when dealing with dark places. You have to see or at least conceive of where you want to go. So, you can't go from your closet to a different closet across town. If you want to teleport within the closet, go crazy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:17:45-07:00","id":556235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=555927#post555927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suddenly feel the need to point out that despite my detailed analysis I was not accepting &quot;night&quot; as a &quot;shadow&quot; for the purposes of the power. I was explaining why even if you accept the ludicrous premise then you still fail. I say it works in a dark cave because it's dark. It works at night with a new moon and no lights for the same reason. That fits what seems to be the intention in a more narrow fashion than it is stated. I don't remember if the power states you have to see where you intend to go, but I would consider that the case when dealing with dark places. You have to see or at least conceive of where you want to go. So, you can't go from your closet to a different closet across town. If you want to teleport within the closet, go crazy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Heres the whole thing<br /> <br /> The Beast deepens her communion with the darkness, which can transport<br /> her wherever it touches.<span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For the rest of the scene, she can step into a shadow and \u201cteleport\u201d to<br /> another shadow anywhere in sight</span>,</span></span>assuming it is large enough to hold her. She can use this<br /> ability either while physical or in shadow form. Depending on the circumstances, the Beast can<br /> cross huge distances in a matter of minutes, all without being seen. This ability is in addition to<br /> the normal and low Satiety effects<br /> <br /> So yeah you have to have sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:59:33-07:00","id":556307,"title":"","content":"I thought I remembered reading that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:16:13-07:00","id":556647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=550775#post550775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, also, Does the Shadow count as a shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Who knows what evil lurks in the hearts of men? The Shadow knows...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T01:13:51-07:00","id":556668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556647#post556647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Who knows what evil lurks in the hearts of men? The Shadow knows...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/KVWXGUl.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T05:02:36-07:00","id":556764,"title":"","content":"Here's the fun part - can you step into one of the strix and teleport? They're literally made of shadows!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T05:11:26-07:00","id":556769,"title":"","content":"Actually once they get powerful enough they can shadow jump themselves. Can they use <i>each other</i> as portals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:04:38-07:00","id":556802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=555896#post555896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because what the average person means in casual conversation by the word 'shadow' does not encompass the huge honking shadow of the Earth blotting out the Sun that we refer to as 'night'. We've got a separate word for it and everything. Although it is objectively just a big shadow it's rare that supernatural powers treat it that way. For instance, Vampires take damage from the sun even when they're standing in shadows, which by the logic employed here should mean that going outside EVER should kill them. (and in fact, many places inside as well.)<br /> <br /> There should be a note precisely <i>because</i> the application of it is ludicrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because the average person does not understand that night is simply nothing more than one big giant shadow does not invalidate that fact. *shrug*<br /> <br /> As for the comparison of scientific fact vs. the mystical connections associated with the various abilities of creatures attributed my myth and legend, they are often a morass of contradictions when looked at in comparison. Your vampire example is one of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-16-2015, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:29:39-07:00","id":556826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556802#post556802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because the average person does not understand that night is simply nothing more than one big giant shadow does not invalidate that fact. *shrug*<br /> <br /> As for the comparison of scientific fact vs. the mystical connections associated with the various abilities of creatures attributed my myth and legend, they are often a morass of contradictions when looked at in comparison. Your vampire example is one of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a physicist, my opinion is that you should never let physics get in the way of your enjoyment of your own make-believe.<br /> These are magical monsters who deploy magic, to do magic all done in a make-believe world entirely subject to the whims of the players and Storyteller who create it. If something isn't contributing to the fun, shove it.<br /> <br /> A fun example of this, was when I calculated that several of the &quot;run really fast&quot; powers that some supernaturals have, could concievably be used to let a character break the sound barrier while sprinting. Thats not something a person can survive without shielding, much less keep his eyes open to navigate and avoid running full tilt into everything. Eventually he might even catch on fire from air friction.<br /> Theres also the cases in which the &quot;jump really high&quot; powers causes simmilar effects, with breaking the sound barrier, but also causes the characters leg-bones to shatter horrificly during take-off and the imminent death of that character, since the power doesn't explitly state that it shields the character from fall damage.<br /> <br /> My point is, theres a reason why RPG systems use abstract die-pool mechanics to simmulate physical scenarioes. It would be easy to put up Newtonian equations to explain how movement works, but considering every minute physical detail really kills the mood of the situation.<br /> Just do whats fun for you, not whats physically correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:41:35-07:00","id":556845,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, a shadow is generally not considered to include the shaded part of the object causing it. <br /> <br /> Like, if you cast a shadow, your shadow is the bit on the ground, not the entire side of you facing away from the light source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:44:08-07:00","id":556848,"title":"","content":"No doubt... I agree that physics often gets in the way of RPG games (your examples are highly entertaining, <i><b>Krobeles</b></i>), due to a lot of various reasons. However, I have found that often people's experiences add to the enjoyment of a game. Equations notwithstanding, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From my experience in Mage (Ascension at least - never played Awakening) it often was the case that the person with the best underlying understanding of physics and science ended up being the best mage overall. Not because he argued for the most accurate understanding of Science (which we stomped on relentlessly and with utter and absolute prejudice), but because he UNDERSTOOD the rules which he was trying to break with Magic (or apply with Magic as was often the case).<br /> <br /> Fact is... &quot;Shadow&quot; and &quot;Night&quot; are no different, they are the absence of light due to the light being blocked (from one thing or another). Metaphysically you might argue they are different, but in reality, that is simply semantics. Wanna Jump all over the place in the Night (with line of sight)? Knock yourself out. It won't really make all that much difference, really. Definitely not as disruptive as many Mage abilities, in my opinion. *shrug* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:46:14-07:00","id":556849,"title":"","content":"We're dealing with powers derived from the astral realm. Semantics is important here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:47:02-07:00","id":556851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556849#post556849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're dealing with powers derived from the astral realm. Semantics is important here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T07:50:36-07:00","id":556880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556848#post556848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No doubt... I agree that physics often gets in the way of RPG games (your examples are highly entertaining, <i><b>Krobeles</b></i>), due to a lot of various reasons. However, I have found that often people's experiences add to the enjoyment of a game. Equations notwithstanding, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From my experience in Mage (Ascension at least - never played Awakening) it often was the case that the person with the best underlying understanding of physics and science ended up being the best mage overall. Not because he argued for the most accurate understanding of Science (which we stomped on relentlessly and with utter and absolute prejudice), but because he UNDERSTOOD the rules which he was trying to break with Magic (or apply with Magic as was often the case).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found this to be the case as well, and it's something I love about playing magic users in general and Mage in specific. (I <i>am</i> That Guy for my group, at least when I'm not the one running the game.) Understanding the mechanics of what you're attempting to do is always going to give you an edge, whether it's simple leverage or employing the Principle of Similarity and some runes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556848#post556848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fact is... &quot;Shadow&quot; and &quot;Night&quot; are no different, they are the absence of light due to the light being blocked (from one thing or another). Metaphysically you might argue they are different, but in reality, that is simply semantics. Wanna Jump all over the place in the Night (with line of sight)? Knock yourself out. It won't really make all that much difference, really. Definitely not as disruptive as many Mage abilities, in my opinion. *shrug* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow and night are no different in the sense of the physical mechanics of why there is no light, but the semantics <i>matter</i> here. My point wasn't mainly that there's some kind of metaphysical delineation between the two but that the person who actually wrote the power almost certainly did not intend for it to be interpreted in a way that treats night as a gigantic shadow because if they had it would SAY so. Not because there's some kind of magic logic involved, but because otherwise the first time someone tries to teleport to the moon with it you get this entire thread worth of arguing.<br /> <br /> What I was trying to illustrate (badly, it seems) with the vampire example was that you're very rarely going to see someone in the Requiem forums arguing that moonlight should be fatal to vampires in the RAW because it says indirect sunlight causes harm and moonlight is literally nothing indirect sunlight. The <i>reason</i> you don't see that argument popping up all the time is that it's understood that because the author didn't explicitly include moonlight as an example and it's treated as a separate thing in casual language it is it is meant to be treated as a separate thing. So it is with night vs. shadow. Physically they are 'the absence of light created by an opaque object obstructing its path' but you don't have people arguing that an overcast day and twilight are the same thing.<br /> <br /> If you want a metaphysical justification... heck, there's a lot of them. The simplest one is just that where Science is one way of labeling and analyzing the world, Magic is another and in the WoD when they conflict it's generally the magical answer that is the correct one for most purposes. In Mage sunlight and light are treated as such distinct things that it requires a substantially higher Forces rating to manipulate sunlight, which is patently absurd from a physics standpoint. (As is the fact that it is easier to convert a hamster into a machine gun than it is to turn lead into gold.) A vampire who would burn to ashes in seconds simply because they were on the far side of the room when someone opened the blinds can go for a moonlit stroll with no discomfort at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> For game purposes, my personal ruling for what constitutes a 'shadow' is going to be a patch of darkness that is visibly distinct from the surrounding light level on the relevant surface. That is, if someone who isn't being a pedant would look at it and consider it a shadow as opposed to just generally dark, it'll count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T08:03:48-07:00","id":556897,"title":"","content":"Ya'll do realize that even with all this talk, ultimately you can just shine a flashlight at the moon, wave a piece of paper over it, and bam. To the moon?<br /> <br /> It's really, extremely, not a problem. I mean, how many situations can be solved by randomly going to the moon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T08:11:49-07:00","id":556904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556897#post556897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya'll do realize that even with all this talk, ultimately you can just shine a flashlight at the moon, wave a piece of paper over it, and bam. To the moon? It's really, extremely, not a problem. I mean, how many situations can be solved by randomly going to the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC it has to be a connected shadow and you definitely have to be able to see it, so actually you can't.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm less concerned about teleporting to the moon in specific and more about the ability to get to any given point on about half the planet instantly as a casual exercise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T08:25:49-07:00","id":556911,"title":"","content":"No, it doesn't have to be connected. Strictly speaking that wouldn't be a different shadow at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T08:39:48-07:00","id":556918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556911#post556911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it doesn't have to be connected. Strictly speaking that wouldn't be a different shadow at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I stand corrected. I was thinking 'shadow of a distinct object that is overlapping another' although it would be a weird way to define things, admittedly. Not sure why I was thinking that was in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:21:56-07:00","id":556989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556897#post556897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya'll do realize that even with all this talk, ultimately you can just shine a flashlight at the moon, wave a piece of paper over it, and bam. To the moon?<br /> <br /> It's really, extremely, not a problem. I mean, how many situations can be solved by randomly going to the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then it would be questionable whether you would be able to see the shadow. Even if you had some kind of magnification, the piece of paper will just not project a visible shadow from this large distance when using a flashlight.<br /> <br /> Maybe a very strong laser with a thick beam could solve this problem, but that seems to be more trouble than it's worth. Especially as that will be very visible to the people on Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:49:26-07:00","id":557014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556989#post556989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even then it would be questionable whether you would be able to see the shadow. Even if you had some kind of magnification, the piece of paper will just not project a visible shadow from this large distance when using a flashlight.<br /> <br /> Maybe a very strong laser with a thick beam could solve this problem, but that seems to be more trouble than it's worth. Especially as that will be very visible to the people on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I refer you here: <a href=\"https://what-if.xkcd.com/13/\" target=\"_blank\">https://what-if.xkcd.com/13/</a><br /> (Short version: there's not a snowballs chance in Hell that you'd be able to see it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:10:07-07:00","id":557069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557014#post557014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I refer you here: <a href=\"https://what-if.xkcd.com/13/\" target=\"_blank\">https://what-if.xkcd.com/13/</a><br /> (Short version: there's not a snowballs chance in Hell that you'd be able to see it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read that one before. It is not really comparable to my point as I assumed magnification (maybe too explicitly). The article says nothing about focussing a decent laser at one spot (which will still result in a beam of about two kilometers wide with a really good laser), and trying to pick up on the diffusing light. But I agree that it is implausible that you would be able to see something through a telescope.<br /> <br /> You could also launch your shadow creating &quot;lamp-paper apparatus&quot; to the moon, to create your shadow there. Then you only have to worry about creating a shadow of a few kilometers in diameter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:22:35-07:00","id":557107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=555859#post555859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should there be a note on commonly accepted scientific knowledge? The application of it may be ludicrous, but still...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's common scientific knowledge that moonlight is just reflected Light from the Sun. Doesn't kill Vampires does it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:25:50-07:00","id":557114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556897#post556897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya'll do realize that even with all this talk, ultimately you can just shine a flashlight at the moon, wave a piece of paper over it, and bam. To the moon?<br /> <br /> It's really, extremely, not a problem. I mean, how many situations can be solved by randomly going to the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't cast a shadow on the moon. The diffusion of light is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T12:00:47-07:00","id":557185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557107#post557107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's common scientific knowledge that moonlight is just reflected Light from the Sun. Doesn't kill Vampires does it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually knew a guy once who ran his setting that way. In addition vampires were also directly harmed by things considered holy or sacred regardless of faith, which caused problems once I pointed out that there are faiths that just view nature in general as sacred. The only explanation I could get from him on why vampires weren't flat out extinct basically amounted to them being literally impossible to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T12:20:02-07:00","id":557193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557107#post557107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's common scientific knowledge that moonlight is just reflected Light from the Sun. Doesn't kill Vampires does it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but all a vampire need do is stay in the shadows of the resultant Moonlight and they are just fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T12:22:02-07:00","id":557194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=556848#post556848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No doubt... I agree that physics often gets in the way of RPG games (your examples are highly entertaining, <i><b>Krobeles</b></i>), due to a lot of various reasons. However, I have found that often people's experiences add to the enjoyment of a game. Equations notwithstanding, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From my experience in Mage (Ascension at least - never played Awakening) it often was the case that the person with the best underlying understanding of physics and science ended up being the best mage overall. Not because he argued for the most accurate understanding of Science (which we stomped on relentlessly and with utter and absolute prejudice), but because he UNDERSTOOD the rules which he was trying to break with Magic (or apply with Magic as was often the case).<br /> <br /> Fact is... &quot;Shadow&quot; and &quot;Night&quot; are no different, they are the absence of light due to the light being blocked (from one thing or another). Metaphysically you might argue they are different, but in reality, that is simply semantics. Wanna Jump all over the place in the Night (with line of sight)? Knock yourself out. It won't really make all that much difference, really. Definitely not as disruptive as many Mage abilities, in my opinion. *shrug* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of something I thought of years ago: If an Obrimos were to use the Forces Arcanum spell (I forget what level) that lets you effectively transfer energy (specifically heat) from one area to another to move all of the heat in and around one person's body to the body of anther person, what happens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T12:37:37-07:00","id":557218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557194#post557194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me of something I thought of years ago: If an Obrimos were to use the Forces Arcanum spell (I forget what level) that lets you effectively transfer energy (specifically heat) from one area to another to move all of the heat in and around one person's body to the body of anther person, what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on what you consider to be <i>all</i> of the heat. If we're talking 'temperature drops to 0C (or F, take your pick) then you've increased the body temperature of one person uniformly to WAY above the level that it'll kill them and the other to a low enough temperature that all the water in their body will freeze, which will also kill them. It wouldn't <i>look</i> like much (maybe a flush and some frost, respectively) but they'd both be corpses in seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:11:57-07:00","id":557231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557218#post557218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Depends on what you consider to be <i>all</i> of the heat. If we're talking 'temperature drops to 0C (or F, take your pick) then you've increased the body temperature of one person uniformly to WAY above the level that it'll kill them and the other to a low enough temperature that all the water in their body will freeze, which will also kill them. It wouldn't <i>look</i> like much (maybe a flush and some frost, respectively) but they'd both be corpses in seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are mostly water, so we'll assume that humans are entirely water.<br /> <br /> An average adult human has a mass of about 81 kilograms, and its baseline temperature is 310.15 Kelvins (or 37 degrees Celsius/98.6 degrees Fahrenheit).<br /> Water has a specific heat of 4.187 kilojoules per kilogram-Kelvin.<br /> Using the formula Q=m*c*dT, we can calculate thermal energy in Joules (Q), based on mass in kilograms (m), specific heat in kJ/kg*K (c), and change in temperature (dT)<br /> m is already established as 81 kg.<br /> c is the specific heat, 4.187 kJ/kg*K<br /> dT is 310.15 Kelvins, because we're wanting <i>all</i> the thermal energy in the person.<br /> Q = 81 <s>kg</s> * 4.187 kJ/<s>kg*K</s> * 310.15 <s>K</s>--&gt;cancel units<br /> Q = 81 * 4.187 kJ * 310.15--&gt;Arithmetic<br /> Q = 105186.44205 kJ<br /> How much energy is a hundred thousand kilojoules?<ul><li>According to Wolfram Alpha: 79% of the energy in a gallon of gas.</li> <li>1.7 times the amount of energy needed to accelerate 1 kg to escape velocity from Earth (ignoring drag)</li> <li>2.5 times the energy consumed daily by &lt;ichael Phelps while training for the Olympics</li> <li>Equivalent to annihilating 1.2 micrograms of matter as per E=mc<sup>2</sup></li> </ul>So, quite a bit of thermal energy, but not as much as one might assume.<br /> If you account for the calories contained in bodily tissue, it becomes a much bigger number, but I'm not doing the math for that unless somebody asks me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:17:46-07:00","id":557238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557231#post557231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, quite a bit of thermal energy, but not as much as one might assume.<br /> If you account for the calories contained in bodily tissue, it becomes a much bigger number, but I'm not doing the math for that unless somebody asks me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Could you calculate the energy if someone made all of the Sun's rays that pass within a hundred yards of the target redirect towards that person? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:20:24-07:00","id":557262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557193#post557193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, but all a vampire need do is stay in the shadows of the resultant Moonlight and they are just fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire need do nothin because they are unaffected by Moon light. If you want to ignore how the game actually works that fine, but act like that's how it is supposed to work by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:25:29-07:00","id":557264,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected. I confused low satiety conditions and satiety expenditure conditions, so you could in fact teleport to the moon. You would immediately begin taking aggravated damage each turn until you teleported back. You have your current health in turns before you die to leave the moon. Of course, I guess you could sneak into NASA and steal a spacesuit. I guess I will not have to go with throwing dice at the player for this one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:41:27-07:00","id":557297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557262#post557262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A vampire need do nothin because they are unaffected by Moon light. If you want to ignore how the game actually works that fine, but act like that's how it is supposed to work by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow... Just Wow... playful sarcasm just totally escapes you doesn't it?<br /> Well, then, carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-16-2015, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T14:09:47-07:00","id":557314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557238#post557238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome! Could you calculate the energy if someone made all of the Sun's rays that pass within a hundred yards of the target redirect towards that person? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't have the hard numbers, but a one meter wide Fresnel lens can focus sunlight down to a point that reaches ~3000F. At a hundred times that much energy, you'd blast a hole clear through your target and very likely whatever was on the far side of them at the very least. I suspect that the radiant heat generated by whatever slag was left (and the air your Death Star incantation had passed through) would be superheated enough to make being anywhere near it profoundly uncomfortable and possibly fatal. Malonkey1 can probably give a more rigorous answer as he's either substantially better versed in physics than I am or he's got a lot more patience for that kind of incidental research. (or both.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T14:12:08-07:00","id":557315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557231#post557231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans are mostly water, so we'll assume that humans are entirely water.<br /> <br /> An average adult human has a mass of about 81 kilograms, and its baseline temperature is 310.15 Kelvins (or 37 degrees Celsius/98.6 degrees Fahrenheit).<br /> Water has a specific heat of 4.187 kilojoules per kilogram-Kelvin.<br /> Using the formula Q=m*c*dT, we can calculate thermal energy in Joules (Q), based on mass in kilograms (m), specific heat in kJ/kg*K (c), and change in temperature (dT)<br /> m is already established as 81 kg.<br /> c is the specific heat, 4.187 kJ/kg*K<br /> dT is 310.15 Kelvins, because we're wanting <i>all</i> the thermal energy in the person.<br /> Q = 81 <s>kg</s> * 4.187 kJ/<s>kg*K</s> * 310.15 <s>K</s>--&gt;cancel units<br /> Q = 81 * 4.187 kJ * 310.15--&gt;Arithmetic<br /> Q = 105186.44205 kJ<br /> How much energy is a hundred thousand kilojoules?<ul><li>According to Wolfram Alpha: 79% of the energy in a gallon of gas.</li> <li>1.7 times the amount of energy needed to accelerate 1 kg to escape velocity from Earth (ignoring drag)</li> <li>2.5 times the energy consumed daily by &lt;ichael Phelps while training for the Olympics</li> <li>Equivalent to annihilating 1.2 micrograms of matter as per E=mc<sup>2</sup></li> </ul>So, quite a bit of thermal energy, but not as much as one might assume.<br /> If you account for the calories contained in bodily tissue, it becomes a much bigger number, but I'm not doing the math for that unless somebody asks me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for fielding the specifics. =) I specified the 37C temperature point mainly to clarify that by 'all the heat' I assumed he didn't mean 'chills the target to 0 kelvin', which would be a much more pronounced change.<br /> <br /> (Also physically impossible, but this IS magic we're talking about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T18:23:54-07:00","id":557681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557218#post557218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Depends on what you consider to be <i>all</i> of the heat. If we're talking 'temperature drops to 0C (or F, take your pick) then you've increased the body temperature of one person uniformly to WAY above the level that it'll kill them and the other to a low enough temperature that all the water in their body will freeze, which will also kill them. It wouldn't <i>look</i> like much (maybe a flush and some frost, respectively) but they'd both be corpses in seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was thinking. Not super dramatic, (covert?) but a real puzzle for the coroner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:44:25-07:00","id":558178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557681#post557681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I was thinking. Not super dramatic, (covert?) but a real puzzle for the coroner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much <i>anyone</i> killed by a mage is going to be confusing as hell for the poor coroner if they do an autopsy. &quot;Well your honor... on examination, Victim A appeared to have developed fatal osteoporosis despite being an otherwise healthy 24 year old male, Victim B had a potted fern where their heart should have been, and Victim C was charred beyond recognition but we couldn't find any trace of accelerants.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":1647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","user":"Mechalith","date":". 06-17-2015, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:26:26-07:00","id":558828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=558178#post558178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much <i>anyone</i> killed by a mage is going to be confusing as hell for the poor coroner if they do an autopsy. &quot;Well your honor... on examination, Victim A appeared to have developed fatal osteoporosis despite being an otherwise healthy 24 year old male, Victim B had a potted fern where their heart should have been, and Victim C was charred beyond recognition but we couldn't find any trace of accelerants.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but victims B and C would clearly be Vulgar effects in 1e, while victim A could be explained as a rare, previously undiagnosed hereditary condition.<br /> <br /> Question: How far could a Mage shift energy from one place to another? Touch range? Sensory? Scyring? A man dies from hypothermia outdoors in winter, and another boils alive in a Jacuzzi miles away...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:57:25-07:00","id":558864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=558828#post558828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but victims B and C would clearly be Vulgar effects in 1e, while victim A could be explained as a rare, previously undiagnosed hereditary condition.<br /> <br /> Question: How far could a Mage shift energy from one place to another? Touch range? Sensory? Scyring? A man dies from hypothermia outdoors in winter, and another boils alive in a Jacuzzi miles away...</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the mage. Due to how mages function and the methods they use these details can change significantly. Like a popular assassination method for one faction in a friends game was basically setting up some things so you could pass as a similar being to the target then downing a liter of some poison and using a second spell to swap it so that suddenly there's a liter of poison coursing through the target's system with you just suffering the damage from it being in your system up until that point. This tended to work from the other side of the planet when they were willing to risk being vulgar enough to not have left standard reality to avoid the inevitable angry hand of god that this tended to provoke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:46:05-07:00","id":559025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557238#post557238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome! Could you calculate the energy if someone made all of the Sun's rays that pass within a hundred yards of the target redirect towards that person? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=557314#post557314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't have the hard numbers, but a one meter wide Fresnel lens can focus sunlight down to a point that reaches ~3000F. At a hundred times that much energy, you'd blast a hole clear through your target and very likely whatever was on the far side of them at the very least. I suspect that the radiant heat generated by whatever slag was left (and the air your Death Star incantation had passed through) would be superheated enough to make being anywhere near it profoundly uncomfortable and possibly fatal. Malonkey1 can probably give a more rigorous answer as he's either substantially better versed in physics than I am or he's got a lot more patience for that kind of incidental research. (or both.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this would be easiest by starting with a set of known numbers:<ul><li>The entire planet gets an average direct insolation of 1000 Watts per square meter.</li> <li>A circle with a radius of 100 yards has an area of 26268 square meters.</li> <li>To get the wattage of this spell, we multiply these two together, giving us 26268000 Watts. That's a lot.</li> <li>To get the energy in Joules, let's break this down. 1 Watt = Joule/s</li> <li>We can assume we want this spell to last 1 turn, but it could be more. 1 turn in Storyteller System is 3 seconds. Multiply 3 seconds by 26268000 Watts. This level of wattage is equivalent to:<ul><li>about 0.2% the power of the Space Shuttle at launch</li> <li>Peak power produced by the reactor of a Los Angeles class nuclear sub</li> <li>69% of the power production of the largest solar power plant in the US</li> </ul></li> <li>This gives us 78.8 million Joules. According to Wolfram Alpha, this is equal to:<ul><li>59% of the energy released by burning 1 gallon of gasoline</li> <li>1.3 times the energy needed to accelerate 1 kg of matter to escape velocity, ignoring drag.</li> </ul></li> <li>If you were able to maintain the spell for 1 minute, and immediately release it, it would be about 106% the energy released by a bolt of lightning.</li> </ul>The verdict? Such a spell would be survivable, but agonizing, would would certainly become lethal if maintained for any real length of time. And if you're a Vampire, you're obviously megadead. (1.088 megadeaths, to be precise).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T23:02:13-07:00","id":559084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=559025#post559025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, this would be easiest by starting with a set of known numbers:<ul><li>The entire planet gets an average direct insolation of 1000 Watts per square meter.</li> <li>A circle with a radius of 100 yards has an area of 26268 square meters.</li> <li>To get the wattage of this spell, we multiply these two together, giving us 26268000 Watts. That's a lot.</li> <li>To get the energy in Joules, let's break this down. 1 Watt = Joule/s</li> <li>We can assume we want this spell to last 1 turn, but it could be more. 1 turn in Storyteller System is 3 seconds. Multiply 3 seconds by 26268000 Watts. This level of wattage is equivalent to:<ul><li>about 0.2% the power of the Space Shuttle at launch</li> <li>Peak power produced by the reactor of a Los Angeles class nuclear sub</li> <li>69% of the power production of the largest solar power plant in the US</li> </ul></li> <li>This gives us 78.8 million Joules. According to Wolfram Alpha, this is equal to:<ul><li>59% of the energy released by burning 1 gallon of gasoline</li> <li>1.3 times the energy needed to accelerate 1 kg of matter to escape velocity, ignoring drag.</li> </ul></li> <li>If you were able to maintain the spell for 1 minute, and immediately release it, it would be about 106% the energy released by a bolt of lightning.</li> </ul><br /> The verdict? Such a spell would be survivable, but agonizing, would would certainly become lethal if maintained for any real length of time. And if you're a Vampire, you're obviously megadead. (1.088 megadeaths, to be precise).</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL! Stealing part of this for my sig!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 06-18-2015, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:47:57-07:00","id":559317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=559025#post559025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, this would be easiest by starting with a set of known numbers:<ul><li>The entire planet gets an average direct insolation of 1000 Watts per square meter.</li> <li>A circle with a radius of 100 yards has an area of 26268 square meters.</li> <li>To get the wattage of this spell, we multiply these two together, giving us 26268000 Watts. That's a lot.</li> <li>To get the energy in Joules, let's break this down. 1 Watt = Joule/s</li> <li>We can assume we want this spell to last 1 turn, but it could be more. 1 turn in Storyteller System is 3 seconds. Multiply 3 seconds by 26268000 Watts. This level of wattage is equivalent to:<ul><li>about 0.2% the power of the Space Shuttle at launch</li> <li>Peak power produced by the reactor of a Los Angeles class nuclear sub</li> <li>69% of the power production of the largest solar power plant in the US</li> </ul></li> <li>This gives us 78.8 million Joules. According to Wolfram Alpha, this is equal to:<ul><li>59% of the energy released by burning 1 gallon of gasoline</li> <li>1.3 times the energy needed to accelerate 1 kg of matter to escape velocity, ignoring drag.</li> </ul></li> <li>If you were able to maintain the spell for 1 minute, and immediately release it, it would be about 106% the energy released by a bolt of lightning.</li> </ul>The verdict? Such a spell would be survivable, but agonizing, would would certainly become lethal if maintained for any real length of time. And if you're a Vampire, you're obviously megadead. (1.088 megadeaths, to be precise).</div> </div> </div> </div>As a somewhat more concrete idea of how much heat energy we're talking about, this is a 30 kilowatt laser <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vXCAWuTZ_MU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vXCAWuTZ_MU</a> (the same power used in the naval lasers they shoot down missiles with)<br /> <br /> With that firmly in mind: the output of this spell would be 875.6 times more energy. You'd live through that, depending on where it hits you, but I can't imagine the damage would be anything less than crippling. The initial target site would be small, but it'd fry a pretty good sized area around it as well. I'm not sure agonizing does the result justice.<br /> <br /> Also, speaking from related experience, it would smell <i>terrible</i>. If you think burning hair is a bad smell, I strongly suggest you avoid ever smelling incinerated human flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:06:22-07:00","id":560265,"title":"","content":"So about shoving someone else through a shadow? Can Namtaru do that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:24:18-07:00","id":560275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=560265#post560265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So about shoving someone else through a shadow? Can Namtaru do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, it appears not. But if a player tried in one of my games, that'd be too f&amp;$kin' cool to refuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:30:09-07:00","id":560280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=560275#post560275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By RAW, it appears not. But if a player tried in one of my games, that'd be too f&amp;$kin' cool to refuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, if Namtaru CAN teleport to the moon, you would be ok with someone using that ability to send people...<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><i><b>TO THE MOOOOON-NAAAHHHH!!!!!</b></i></u> </span><br /> <u><i><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">BEEEEE-YEEEETCH!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</span></b></i></u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 06-19-2015, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:27:11-07:00","id":560349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=559317#post559317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a somewhat more concrete idea of how much heat energy we're talking about, this is a 30 kilowatt laser <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vXCAWuTZ_MU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vXCAWuTZ_MU</a> (the same power used in the naval lasers they shoot down missiles with)<br /> <br /> With that firmly in mind: the output of this spell would be 875.6 times more energy. You'd live through that, depending on where it hits you, but I can't imagine the damage would be anything less than crippling. The initial target site would be small, but it'd fry a pretty good sized area around it as well. I'm not sure agonizing does the result justice.<br /> <br /> Also, speaking from related experience, it would smell <i>terrible</i>. If you think burning hair is a bad smell, I strongly suggest you avoid ever smelling incinerated human flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering an average lightning bolt is on the order of 1 terrawatt, the damage would not be as severe as you might imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:32:28-07:00","id":560669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/550434-namtaru-can-teleport-to-the-moon?p=560349#post560349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering an average lightning bolt is on the order of 1 terrawatt, the damage would not be as severe as you might imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lightning bolt doesn't deliver it's entire charge to a single focused point, and light doesn't pass through flesh the way electricity does, so a lot of the energy in a lightning strike goes someplace other than the person hit with it. Even so, being hit by lightning is usually fatal, and the people it doesn't kill generally don't have a lot of positive things to say about the experience.<br /> <br /> Overall the results would be a lot less extreme than I'd initially estimated, but they'd still be pretty ugly.<br /> <br /> Regardless, enough thread derailing from me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:57:37-07:00","id":563313,"title":"","content":"Ok so i have looked over this and there are two parts for moving through shadows, One is if they touch and yes night time is a shadow cast by the earth and if you can touch that shadow you can then use it but if you take the concept of a lamp and a ball the dark side of the ball is not the shadow, the shadow is the object behind the earth which the shadow is on. But one could argue that anything in the dark side would be an object which the shadow is cast on, but you must remember the one part to this. The shadows must connect so if you think crossing the ocean is going to work i will tell you no the sky does count as a shadow but object on the land would. If one is on a moonless night in the ocean one can that shadows are not connected as the night sky would break that with the reflection of the sky, and if you use the storm one bolt of lighting could disconnect you as it counts as bright light. So if you melt into the shadow of the earth you are consider the whole shadow and spot lights or lighting will break the effect. One would not want to be in the ocean miles from shore. Now to counter that if you shadow step to the coast and then swim in to the darkness of the sea and then you can cross but that multiple connections. And on the second part of this power by spending Satiety point which is too be the most powerful effect requires you to have line of sight. To the moon is a shadow you can see which is not connected to anything so you would have to spend a point to get there but with out a space suit or effect equal to the vacuum of space and the science behind what happens to your body in space would kill you by one of the following effects: Pressure, boiling water from inside you, lack of air to breath, the epic coldness, and just for fun some supernatural hand that would come out and smack you for that foolish attempt. But if you are an astronaut and have access to this mundane equipment or have supernatural friends who could help you avoid the effects then yes your can pop up there and see all the shadows on the dark side of the earth and pop back. So in conclusion you can hop around the world by multiple connection and yes you can go to the moon and die if you want. But there is always someone out there who can to the same thing they are called mages.<br /> <br /> This power does need it limitations in my opinion such as lair rating X (10)miles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":3293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","user":"Rahod","date":". 06-21-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:06:38-07:00","id":563471,"title":"","content":"Sure, teleport to the moon. I don't know if I'd want to see what a moon bound Idigam would do with the soul of a Beast it was able to strip it from. Then again...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:46:48-07:00","id":564828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum